# First task next session: what-if freight & tariff adjusters

Do this **before** other new Finance/what-if work.

## Goal
In the Costing **what-if** model, allow adjusting:
- Freight in ($/lb and/or $/kg)
- Tariff rate

## Critical constraint — do not double-count
Cost Master **landed** cost already includes estimated freight-in and tariff (see `CostMaster` landed calc: price × (1 + tariff) + freight, then $/lb).

What-if must treat that landed figure as the baseline, then let the user model **deltas** or **replacement** assumptions without adding freight/tariff on top of a cost that already embeds them.

Prefer one clear approach (document in UI help text):
- Start from **ex-works / base price** when user edits freight & tariff, **or**
- Start from **landed** and treat freight/tariff fields as **adjustments vs embedded estimates** (net add/remove), never raw re-add of the same Cost Master freight/tariff already inside landed.

## Touch points (expected)
- `backend_django/slurp_ui/pricing_whatif.py`
- `backend_django/slurp_ui/templates/slurp_ui/finance/_whatif.html` (+ `_whatif_js.html`)
- `PricingWhatIfLine` model/migration if persisting freight/tariff fields
- Cost Master fields: `freight_per_kg`, `tariff`, `landed_cost_per_lb`, `price_per_lb` / `price_per_kg`

## Done when
User can scrub freight and tariff on a what-if row, see price/GP update live, and Cost Master landed components are not counted twice.

After implementing, **delete or cancel this rule** so it does not stick forever.
